.TH WHOIS 1
.SH NAME
whois \- query a whois server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whois
.RB [ -a
.IR addr ]
.RB [ -n ]
.I host
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Whois
looks up
.I host
and prints the response. It starts at IANA's own whois server and
follows any
.B refer:
line in the reply to the right regional registry automatically, up to
five hops.
.TP 10
.BI -a " addr"
Query
.I addr
instead of the default (IANA) server.
.TP
.B -n
Don't follow
.B refer:
lines; print whatever the first server queried returns.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/whois.b
